    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòúbòúléŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòúbòúwé</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòúbòúléŋ_215_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte de tubercule sauvage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>type of wild tuber</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 24: bòúbòúléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòúwó_216">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòúwó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòúláŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòúwó_216_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gros intestin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>large intestine</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 25: bòúwó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòùwɔ̀ɔ́_217">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòùwɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bòùwɔ̀ɔ́_217_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>couper, casser un morceau (à la machette, avec les dents) ; enlever</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cut or break off a piece (with a machete or the teeth); remove</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.3 Cut"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 25: bòùwɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boŋaa_218">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boŋaa_218_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire trébucher ; piège ; talocher (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make stumble; snare; slap (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.1 Hit"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>trip, stumble, stub one's toe; knock, strike</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Bonhaa; Childs 2000, p. 23: bòŋɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, pow boŋaa « pierre d'achoppement, piège » (JDG 2,3 ; ISA 8,14) et boŋnin « (ne) trébuchera (pas) » (PSA 62,3). Le sens « talocher » de Keita correspond au bɔ̀ŋàá « frapper » de Childs (p. 22).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòŋbòŋndó_219">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòŋbòŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòŋbòŋndá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòŋbòŋndó_219_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce d'oiseau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>species of bird</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 22: bòŋbòŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boŋiboŋio_220">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋiboŋio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋiboŋi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boŋiboŋio_220_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chanceler, tituber</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stagger, totter, keep stumbling</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>keep stubbing one's toe</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 2SA.22.46; Childs 2000, p. 22: bòŋìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Redoublement de boŋio. vana-vana co boŋiboŋi le « personne ne chancelle » (ISA.5.27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boŋio_221">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boŋinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boŋio_221_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>trébucher, buter (plusieurs, ou à plusieurs reprises)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stumble, trip (of several, or repeatedly)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first PSA.9.4; Childs 2000, p. 22: bòŋìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel verbal de boŋ « trébucher » : boŋndo o boŋ « il trébuche » (JHN.11.10) ; boŋilan « fautes, faux pas » (JAS.3.2). Voir boŋaa « faire trébucher ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bùáá_222">
