      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 43 occurrences, first GEN.31.19</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciimiaa_429">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciimiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciimiaa_429_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>écraser, piétiner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>crush, trample</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.6 Grind"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>rub with the hands, press, squeeze (plural of cììmàá)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 12 occurrences, first 2KI.8.12; Childs 2000, p. 46: cììmìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciindiaa_430">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciindiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ciindiaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ciindiaa_430_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sauver, secourir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>save, rescue</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>wean (a child); survive, make survive, rescue</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 238 occurrences, first GEN.6.18; Childs 2000, p. 48: cìndàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciindian_431">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciindian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciindian_431_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se sauver soi-même ; (pila ciindian) se sauver</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>save oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first MAT.27.40; Childs 2000, p. 46: cììndìáŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de ciindiaa « sauver ». nɔm pila ciindian « sauve-toi toi-même » (MAT.27.40, MAT.27.42).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciinun_432">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciinun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciinun_432_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dévoiler, révéler (son cœur) ; anéantir ; (pila ciinun labɛɛ) se déshonorer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>open up, reveal (one's heart); wipe out; (pila ciinun labɛɛ) dishonour oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be finished, come to an end; lose all self-respect</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first LEV.18.10; Childs 2000, p. 46: cììnɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Samsɔn ciinun kɔl ya o ba « Samson m'a ouvert tout son cœur » (JDG.16.18) ; nɔm pila ciinun labɛɛ « tu te déshonores » (EZK.22.16, LEV.18.10) ; n kɔ ciinun vanaa-mangalaa-isɔɔa ha « anéantissons ces nations » (PSA.83.5). Moyen de cii « finir ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cììpùùwó_433">
