    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cimbulun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cimbullon_442_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>épines, ronces</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thorns, briers</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.2 Bush, shrub"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.5.6; Childs 2000, p. 48: cìmbùllé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel. cimbulun co o lɛŋnde veselɛilen nin-ndon a siɛmbullon « les épines du désert et les ronces » (JDG.8.7, JDG.8.16) ; ISA.5.6.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cimbɔɔ_443">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cimbɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="cimbɔɔ_443_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'enfuir, se sauver (de chez son maître)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>run away, flee (from one's master)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>flee, run away; steal</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1SA.25.10; Childs 2000, p. 48: cìmbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cɛa ... cimbɔɔ o ba mà kɔannun « des esclaves qui s'enfuient de chez leurs maîtres » (1SA.25.10). Seule occurrence. Voir ciimbuu « voler ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cìmèìyó_444">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cìmèìyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cìmèìyó_444_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vendredi (jour du marché sierra-léonais)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>Friday (Sierra Leone market day)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 48: cìmèìyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cindaa_445">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cindaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cinda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cindaa_445_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vie ; salut</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>life; salvation</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6 Life"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(verb) wean; remain alive, survive; rescue</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 172 occurrences, first GEN.2.9; Childs 2000, p. 48: cìndàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciŋ_446">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciŋ_446_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>clairement, de ses propres yeux (cɔu ciŋ, a lehɔl ciŋ)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>clearly, with one's own eyes (cɔu ciŋ, a lehɔl ciŋ)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 32 occurrences, first GEN.45.12</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cíŋ_447">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cíŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cíŋ_447_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fixement, attentivement (regarder)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>intently, keenly (looking)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 49: cíŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciŋaa_448">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ciŋaa_448_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>disposer, arranger (le bois) ; attiser (le feu) ; atteindre (un total)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lay, arrange (wood); stoke (a fire); reach (a total)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>join the edges of, push together; put one's mouth to a cup, drink; stoke a fire; argue in court; add money to a partial payment</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 49: cìŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>yinnden ciŋaa « faire du feu » (Es 40,16) ; vɔsila lan la ciŋa kɛmɛ lehiɔɔlu a beleyaa « au bout de 430 ans » (Ex 12,41). ciŋan : má ciŋan le kolɔɔ « ils se penchèrent pour boire » (Jg 7,6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciŋan_449">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ciŋanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ciŋan_449_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>toucher, joindre ; boire en approchant la bouche (de l'eau) ; (yinnde ciŋanin) cuire sur le feu</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>touch, join; drink by putting the mouth to (water); (fire) be stoked</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.2 Join, attach"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.2 Eat"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>join edges; put the mouth to (water), drink; plead not guilty</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first EXO.25.26; Childs 2000, p. 49: cìŋǎŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de ciŋaa. má ciŋan le kolɔɔ « ils s'agenouillèrent pour boire » (JDG.7.6) ; kumban ... ciŋan a cìì cɛi « l'aile touchait le mur » (2CH.3.11) ; yinnde n ciŋanin a poola « un feu alimenté d'excréments » (EZK.4.12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
