      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>guêpe forestière à piqûre douloureuse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>forest wasp with a painful sting</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 88: dɔ̀ndɔ̀kpééyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔ́ndɔ̀ŋ_751">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔ́ndɔ̀ŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="dɔ́ndɔ̀ŋ_751_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en enflant (grossesse, plaie qui s'infecte)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>swelling up (pregnancy, infected sore)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 88: dɔ́ndɔ̀ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔndɔɔ_752">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔndɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔndɔ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="dɔndɔɔ_752_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prêt, emprunt, dette</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>loan, debt</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>loan, credit</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first DEU.23; Childs 2000, p. 88: dɔ́ndɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>niaa cuenin dɔndɔ le « vous n'emprunterez pas » (DEU.28.12) ; Mɛlɛka salanin dɔndɔ kon « le Seigneur rendra ce prêt » (PRO.19.17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔtɔlɔnɔɔ_753">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔtɔlɔnɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔtɔlɔa</text></form></field>
    <sense id="dɔtɔlɔnɔɔ_753_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>docteur, médecin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>doctor</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.1.1 Worker"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first LUK.5.31; Keita 1979, p. 145: Dötölönöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔvɔɔ_754">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔvɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔw</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔaw</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔawnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="dɔvɔɔ_754_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bénir (… duaa)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bless (… duaa)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 104 occurrences, first GEN.17.16</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔwnun_755">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔwnun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔwnɔnndo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔwnɔn</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔawnun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔawnunnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="dɔwnun_755_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>recevoir, obtenir ; (dɔwnun balo) se nourrir de ; (dɔwnun ɲaale) se réjouir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>receive, obtain; (dɔwnun balo) feed on; (dɔwnun ɲaale) rejoice</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.2 Receive"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 183 occurrences, first GEN.1.30</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de dɔvɔɔ (dɔw, dɔaw). baalala niaalan la dɔawnunnin vɔ̀ngɔ̀ « votre travail sera récompensé » (2 Ch 15,7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔ́ŋgú-dɔ́ŋgú_756">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔ́ŋgú-dɔ́ŋgú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="dɔ́ŋgú-dɔ́ŋgú_756_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>longtemps, de façon prolongée ou répétée</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>for a long time, on and on</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.2 Take time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 88: dɔ́ŋgú-dɔ́ŋgú</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔ́ɔ́_757">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="dɔ́ɔ́_757_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Particle"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>alors, dès lors (moment atteint) ; (te … dɔ́ɔ́ pɛ) dès que, aussitôt que</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>then, by then (point reached); (te … dɔ́ɔ́ pɛ) as soon as, once</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.6 Particles"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.5 Relative time"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>as soon as; marks a moment that is now relevant</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 349 occurrences, first GEN.3.5; Childs 2000, p. 88: dɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>te la de dɔ́ɔ́ pɛ … « le jour où vous en mangerez … » (GEN.3.5) ; mí Noe sina dɔ́ɔ́ maa … « Noé sut alors que … » (GEN.8.11).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔɔnanndo_758">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔɔnanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔɔnan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>dɔɔnannin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="dɔɔnanndo_758_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être peu nombreux, être petit ; être le moindre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be few, be small; be the least</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.1 Small"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 32 occurrences, first NUM.36.4</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o hiow dɔɔnanndo-o « le plus petit » (Mt 5,18).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="dɔ́ɔ́ngɔ́ɔ̀_759">
