  <entry id="hòùwáŋ_1092">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hòùwáŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hòùwáŋ_1092_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>potion de feuilles de hòùwó (contre la constipation)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>potion made from hòùwó leaves (for constipation)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 131: hòùwáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hòùwó_1093">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hòùwó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hòùwó_1093_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arbre à bois dur et blanc (construction)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tree with hard white wood (for building)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.3 Building materials"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 131: hòùwó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hovihovio_1094">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hovihovio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hovihovio_1094_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>piquer (à plusieurs reprises)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>prick, pierce (repeatedly)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.5 Make hole, opening"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>prick many times</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JOS.23.13; Childs 2000, p. 131: hòwìhòwìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Une seule occurrence : maa n'yɔɔ le niaa hɔltan hovihovio « comme des épines qui piquent vos yeux » (JOS.23.13). Cf. hɔwvɔɔ « enfoncer ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huinden_1095">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huinden</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="huinden_1095_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gale</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scabies</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 161: Huinden</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. vana ihuindo « galeux » (Lv 21,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huinndon_1096">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huinndon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="huinndon_1096_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gale, maladie de peau (qui démange)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scab, itching skin disease</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>craw-craw, a skin disease with mottled skin; smallpox</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first DEU.28.27; Childs 2000, p. 134: hùíŋndé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel. Une seule occurrence : nààla bondokpalan, huinndon a tɛɛnndan « ulcères, gale et démangeaisons » (DEU.28.27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huinɔnndo_1097">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huinɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>huinan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="huinɔnndo_1097_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se tromper soi-même ; (huinan) se trahir les uns les autres</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>deceive oneself; (huinan) betray one another</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>fool or trick oneself</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JAS.1.22; Childs 2000, p. 134: hùìnɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de huiyo « tromper ». mɛɛ niaa pila co huinɔnndo ni « vous vous trompez vous-mêmes » (JAS.1.22) ; mà huinan « ils se trahiront » (MAT.24.10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hùíyé_1098">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hùíyé</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hùíyé_1098_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sifflement ; (hɔŋ hùíyé) siffler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>whistle, hiss; (hɔŋ hùíyé) whistle, hiss</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.2 Hear"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5 Communication"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a whistle</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first ISA.5.26; Childs 2000, p. 134: hùíyé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o hɔŋ hùíyé le nda veeloo « il siffle pour les appeler » (ISA.5.26) ; mà hɔŋ hùíyé a mɔnɛi « ils siffleront de stupeur » (JER.25.9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huiyo_1099">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hui</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="huiyo_1099_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tromper, trahir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>deceive, betray</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>cheat, deceive; also break a promise</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 22 occurrences, first JDG.16.10; Childs 2000, p. 134: hùìyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hùlìó_1100">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hùlìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hùlìó_1100_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se salir, se couvrir de poussière ; (peau) desquamer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>get dirty or dusty; (skin) flake</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.1 Clean, dirty"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.4 Skin"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 135: hùlìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hullan_1101">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hullan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hullan_1101_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cerveau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>brain</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 131: Hullan; Childs 2000, p. 135: hùlláŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hullo_1102">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hul</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hullo_1102_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>souffler (sur) ; insuffler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blow (on); breathe into</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.2 Air"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.1 Breathe, breath"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>blow on something; also lie to someone</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JOB.4.15; Childs 2000, p. 135: hùllò</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mó hul ndu hoeyii yoomuɛi o tɛɛngun lamilinndon nin « il souffla dans ses narines un souffle de vie » (GEN.2.7) ; mó hul nda « il souffla sur eux » (JHN.20.22) ; hoeiye pum va ya hɔlla hullo « un souffle passa sur mon visage » (JOB.4.15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hulma pɔmbɔan_1103">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hulma pɔmbɔan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hulma pɔmbɔan_1103_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cervelle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>brains (soft matter)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 131: Hulma pömböan</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hulɔɔ_1104">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hulɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hulu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hulɔɔ_1104_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vider, verser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>empty, pour out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>throw away, spill, dump</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.8.7; Keita 1979, p. 110: Hulöö; Childs 2000, p. 135: hùlɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen hulun « se répandre » (2SA 20,10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="humboo_1105">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>humboo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>humbu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>humbon</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="humboo_1105_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>blanc ; (volin humbon) argent (métal)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>white; (volin humbon) silver</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first LEV.13.24; Childs 2000, p. 135: húmbù-</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hunan_1106">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hunan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hunan_1106_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en crue, qui monte (eau) ; (mɛmma hunan) eaux en crue, flot</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rising, in flood (water); (mɛmma hunan) flood waters</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>flooded (mɛŋmà hùùnâŋ 'the flooding water')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JOB.22.16; Childs 2000, p. 137: hùùnâŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>maa mɛmma hunan o peo Nil « comme les eaux du Nil en crue » (JER.46.7). On trouve aussi mɛmma hunaa « le flot, l'inondation » (JOB.27.20, DAN.11.40). Le rattachement à hunɔɔ « venir » ou à hulɔɔ « verser » (Childs) reste à préciser.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hunnun_1107">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hunnun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hunnun_1107_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(hunnun a) emmener, ramener avec soi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(hunnun a) bring along, bring back</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>arrive, come by one's own power</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first GEN.31.26; Childs 2000, p. 137: hùŋnɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de hunɔɔ « venir ». mì n kɔ hunnun a kesu kpema Hala naa « allons ramener l'arche de notre Dieu » (1CH.13.3) ; ma hunnun a nda « tu les as emmenées » (GEN.31.26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hunɔɔ_1108">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hunɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hunnin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hinnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hunɔɔ_1108_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>venir ; (hun a) apporter, amener</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>come ; come; (hun a) bring</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>come, arrive</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 768 occurrences, first GEN.6.17; Keita 1979, p. 114: Hunöö; Childs 2000, p. 136: hùnɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>hin, hinnin : radical négatif. co hunɔɔ + verbe : « être sur le point de ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="húó_1109">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>húó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>húá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="húó_1109_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hibou, chouette</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>owl</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 137: húó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huuluo_1110">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huuluo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>huulu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>huulunin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>huuloo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>huuluu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="huuluo_1110_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sauter, bondir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>jump, leap</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>jump</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first PSA.68.4; Keita 1979, p. 110: Huuluö; Childs 2000, p. 137: hùùlòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit huuluö ; la Bible écrit huuluo. Pluriel huuluu « sauter, franchir, transgresser » (PSA 114,4 ; NUM 22,18).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hùŋgòó_1111">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hùŋgòó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hùŋgòó_1111_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>piler (le grain), premier pilage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pound grain (first of three poundings)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.6 Process harvest"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 136: hùŋgòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hùŋgùlàá_1112">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hùŋgùlàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hùŋgùlàá_1112_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>agrandir, élargir ; exagérer, grossir (une affaire)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>enlarge, widen; exaggerate, blow up (a matter)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2 Big"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 136: hùŋgùlàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="huŋndo_1113">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>huŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>huŋndan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="huŋndo_1113_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bas-fond, marécage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lowland, swamp</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.1 Bodies of water"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.9 Farmland"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>swamp where swamp rice is grown</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 142: Hunndo; Childs 2000, p. 137: hùŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Hunndo ; le pluriel huŋndan (Jb 40,21) et Childs ont ŋ.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ̂_1114">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̂</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ̂_1114_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>souligne le fait de renverser (un liquide)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stresses spilling (a liquid)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 131: hɔ̂</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́bɔ̀_1115">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́bɔ̀</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ́bɔ̀_1115_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>beaucoup, en abondance</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a lot, plentifully</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ́bɔ̀</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́dèíyó_1116">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́dèíyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ́dèíyó_1116_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ordre (commandement)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>order (command)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5 Authority"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ́dèíyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt à l'anglais selon Childs.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔlaa_1117">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔl</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɔlaa_1117_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>visage, face ; (o … hɔl) devant, en présence de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>face; (o … hɔl) before, in the presence of</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.1 Front"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>face; also sky</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 130 occurrences, first GEN.32.31; Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀llá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔlaa piɔ́mndo_1118">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlaa piɔ́mndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hɔlaa piɔ́mndo_1118_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>masque</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mask</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.5 Art"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 144: Hölaa Piömndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Composé non attesté tel quel : hɔlaa « visage », piɔ́mndo « image, idole ». Mots attestés séparément dans la Bible, mais pas cette expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔlla_1119">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlla</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔl</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɔlla_1119_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>face, visage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>face</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>face; sky</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 443 occurrences, first GEN.12.11; Keita 1979, p. 131: Hölla; Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀llá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔllo_1120">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔllo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hɔllo_1120_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bout, extrémité (d'un bâton, d'un sceptre) ; (o … hɔllo) devant, contre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tip, end (of a stick, sceptre); (o … hɔllo) before, against</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.7 End, point"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>point, tip, top, end</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 1SA.14.43; Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀lló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mó pilan tindaa hɔllo « elle toucha le bout du sceptre » (EST.5.2) ; ya vow hɔllo o lɛan nin « j'ai trempé le bout (du bâton) dans le miel » (1SA.14.43) ; o sim Mɛlɛka o hɔllo « (rien ne) tient devant le Seigneur » (PRO.21.30).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔlmaa_1121">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlmaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="hɔlmaa_1121_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Postposition"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(o … hɔlmaa) aux yeux de, au regard de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(o … hɔlmaa) in the eyes of, in the sight of</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
    </sense>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ̀lndɔ̀_1122">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀lndɔ̀</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ̀lndɔ̀_1122_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Postposition"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>près de, entre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>close to, near, between</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5 Location"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀lndɔ̀</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔlten_1123">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlten</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔltan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlte</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔlta</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɔlten_1123_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>œil ; (nɔ hɔlten … coo) veiller sur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>eye ; eye; (nɔ hɔlten … coo) watch over</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 139 occurrences, first GEN.17.18; Keita 1979, p. 131: Hölten; Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀ltéŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́lɔ̀bí_1124">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́lɔ̀bí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ́lɔ̀bí_1124_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>beaucoup, énormément</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a lot, a great deal</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ́lɔ̀bí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔnlesɛnnɔɔ_1125">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔnlesɛnnɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hɔnlesɛnnɔɔ_1125_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>flûtiste</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flute player</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Hönlesènnöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔwvɔɔ_1126">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔwvɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hɔwvɔɔ_1126_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>injecter, enfoncer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>inject, thrust in</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 115: Höwvöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme attestée dans la Bible : hɔw (1SA 2,14, la fourchette enfoncée).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔŋndo_1127">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔŋ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɔŋndo_1127_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>souffler ; sonner (de la trompette)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blow; sound (a trumpet)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.2 Air"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 57 occurrences, first EXO.10.13</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ̌ŋndó_1128">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ̌ŋndó_1128_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte d'oiseau forestier (faisan ?)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of forest bird (pheasant?)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔŋnɔnndo_1129">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔŋnɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hɔŋnɔnndo_1129_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sonner, retentir (trompette)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sound, be blown (trumpet)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.2 Hear"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be blown</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JOS.6.13; Childs 2000, p. 132: hɔ̀ŋnɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de hɔŋndo « souffler, sonner ». bululan la va hɔŋnɔnndo « les trompettes sonnaient » (JOS.6.13).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́ɔ́_1130">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́aa</text></form></field>
    <sense id="hɔ́ɔ́_1130_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enfant (descendant), fils ou fille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>child, offspring</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.3 Birth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 196 occurrences, first GEN.4.1</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́ɔ̀_1131">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́ɔ̀</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́a</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́ɔ̀_1131_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vipère</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>viper, adder</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a poisonous water snake, a kind of adder</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first GEN.49.17; Childs 2000, p. 133: hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ̀ɔ̀néí_1132">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀ɔ̀néí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ̀ɔ̀nóŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="hɔ̀ɔ̀néí_1132_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gratin de riz (au fond de la marmite)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rice crust (at the bottom of the pot)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 133: hɔ̀ɔ̀néí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔɔnuo_1133">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔɔnuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hɔɔnuo_1133_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>désherber, arracher les mauvaises herbes</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weed</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.4 Tend a field"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>weed</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Höönuo; Childs 2000, p. 133: hɔ̀ɔ̀nòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme attestée dans la Bible : hɔɔnuu « arracher (l'ivraie) » (MAT 13,28).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́ɔ́pìó_1134">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́ɔ́pìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="hɔ́ɔ́pìó_1134_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte de serpent (non venimeux)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of snake (non-venomous)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 133: hɔ́ɔ́pìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɔ́ɔ́yɛi_1135">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɔ́ɔ́yɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hɔ́ɔ́yɛi_1135_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>liberté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>freedom</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.6 Status"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 33 occurrences, first EXO.21.2; Keita 1979, p. 148: Hööyèi</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛiyo_1136">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛyaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɛiyo_1136_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vanner ; cribler ; (fɛlɛ hɛyaa) van</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>winnow; sift; (fɛlɛ hɛyaa) winnowing fork</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.6 Process harvest"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>winnow, fan; also flutter; trick, fool</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first RUT.3.2; Childs 2000, p. 122: hɛ̀ìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o co lakɔ ɔrse ndɔɔ lɔɔ a hɛiyo « il va vanner son orge » (RUT.3.2) ; Setana hɛi niaa maa mɛɛ vana hɛi maalon nuaa yɛ « (que) Satan vous passe au crible comme on vanne le blé » (LUK.22.31) ; Fɛlɛ ndɔ hɛyaa « son van » (MAT.3.12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛli_1137">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛli</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɛli_1137_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>choisir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>choose</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 358 occurrences, first GEN.6.2; Childs 2000, p. 122: hɛ̀líó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlihɛlio_1138">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlihɛlio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="hɛlihɛlio_1138_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>trier plusieurs fois</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sort repeatedly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Hèlihèlio</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Redoublement de hɛlio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlio_1139">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛli</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɛlio_1139_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>choisir, trier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>choose, select, sort</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>choose</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 29 occurrences, first EXO.18; Keita 1979, p. 110: Hèlio; Childs 2000, p. 122: hɛ̀lìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlle_1140">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlle</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="hɛlle_1140_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sel</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>salt</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first EXO.30.35; Childs 2000, p. 122: hɛ̀llé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>A bɛnda ma vow hɛlle « vous y mettrez du sel » (LEV.2.13) ; mó saŋ hɛlle o fonda kobio va-o « il sema du sel sur l'emplacement de la ville » (JDG.9.45).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlu_1141">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>helu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hélú</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɛlu_1141_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre, enlever, s'emparer de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take (away), seize</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 63 occurrences, first GEN.20.18</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Vana-vana hélú ndu ya o ba le « personne ne me l'ôte » (Jn 10,18).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlul_1142">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlul</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>hɛlulun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="hɛlul_1142_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>choisir pour (qqn) ; (hɛlulun) se choisir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>choose for (someone); (hɛlulun) choose for oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>select for someone (variant hɛlul)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first EXO.17.9; Childs 2000, p. 122: hɛ̀lìlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de hɛlio « choisir ». Hɛlul naa kuubaa « choisis-nous des hommes » (EXO.17.9) ; nda pila hɛlulun masaa « ils se donnèrent un roi » (2KI.8.20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="hɛlun_1143">
