      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se multiplier, devenir nombreux</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>multiply, increase</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.4 More"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 126 occurrences, first GEN.1.22</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuilio_1758">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuilio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="kuilio_1758_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>culotte, pantalon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>trousers, shorts</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 144: Lèmböö ; Kuilio; Childs 2000, p. 191: kùìlíó kùìlíláŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuilul_1759">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuilul</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuil</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuilu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuilul_1759_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>multiplier, rendre nombreux ; enrichir, combler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>multiply, make numerous; enrich, fill with good things</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.4 More"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be plentiful; also be mashed; harvest</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 9 occurrences, first GEN.17.2; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mì kuilul nɔm polale nɔmnden taw « je multiplierai beaucoup ta descendance » (GEN.17.2) ; mó kuilu nɔm ɲɛ-ɲɛ co ɲɛ kɛndɔɔ (JOB.36.16). Childs donne la base kùìyó « abonder ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuindian_1760">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuindian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuindianndo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuindiannin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuindian_1760_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se heurter, se bousculer ; se pousser (l'un l'autre)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>knock against each other, jostle; push each other</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.1 Hit"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>knock into each other (plural middle of 'hit')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first JER.13.14; Childs 2000, p. 191: kùìndìáŋ-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>A co ŋovian mà kuindian te « ils ne se bousculent pas » (JOL.2.8) ; Mɛɛ pɛndua va kuindianndo ndu o dembe « comme les jumeaux se heurtaient dans son sein » (GEN.25.22).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuindikuindi_1761">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuindikuindi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuindikuindinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuindikuindi_1761_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>frapper à coups répétés, rouer de coups ; encorner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>strike repeatedly, beat; gore</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.1 Hit"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.2 Fight"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first MAT.26.67; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìndìkùìndìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>má kuindikuindi ndu « ils le frappèrent à coups de poing » (MAT.26.67) ; a leelan ndan n kuindikuindinin vanaa cɔvaa Aramiia « avec ces cornes tu frapperas les Araméens » (1KI.22.11). Cf. kundɔɔ « heurter ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùisiei_1762">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùisiei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisii</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kùisiei_1762_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rasoir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>razor</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.1 Cutting tool"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4.3 Care for hair"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first NUM.6.5; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìsìéí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>kùisiei bɛnda mì i kei ndu o lebol te « le rasoir ne passera pas sur sa tête » (NUM.6.5) ; sendinin a kuisii « raser avec un rasoir » (ISA.7.20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuisin_1763">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisin</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisinndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuisin_1763_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dégoûter, devenir odieux à ; avoir en horreur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>disgust, become loathsome to; loathe</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>vomit on oneself</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 9 occurrences, first GEN.37.8; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìsíŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de kuisio « vomir » : X kuisin Y o kɔl « X devient odieux à Y » (2 S 13,15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuisio_1764">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kuisi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuisio_1764_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vomir, rejeter ; (n.) nausée</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>vomit, spew out; (n.) nausea</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2 Body functions"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first NUM.11.20; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìsìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>kuisio bii niaa « vous en aurez la nausée » (Nb 11,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kuiyo_1765">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kuiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kui</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kuiyo_1765_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>caïman, crocodile</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>crocodile</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 31 occurrences, first GEN.6.1; Keita 1979, p. 136: Kuiyo; Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a kuì bɛndu « le grand crocodile » (EZK.29.3) ; ailleurs kuiyo y est un homonyme « accroissement, multiplication » (1CH.27.23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùìyó_1766">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùìyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kùìyó_1766_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>purée de banane plantain, manioc ou patate à l'huile</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mashed plantain, cassava or sweet potato served with oil</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 192: kùìyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kúkpùŋ_1767">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kúkpùŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kúkpùŋ_1767_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>clapotis de l'eau contre la berge</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>slap of water against the bank</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kúkpùŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kúkú_1768">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kúkú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kúkú_1768_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>course rapide</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>running quickly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kúkú</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kulaa_1769">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kulaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kula</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kulanndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kulaa_1769_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rugir, gronder, crier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roar, shout</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.4 Animal actions"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>shout, yell; cheer or jeer</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JER.6.23; Childs 2000, p. 193: kùlàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>A co kulaa maa mɛmma ihɛl « leur voix gronde comme la mer » (JER.6.23) ; a kula pɛ « quand ils rugissent » (ISA.5.29, lions).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùlàwèíyáŋ_1770">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùlàwèíyáŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="ma"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kùlàwèíyáŋ_1770_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>goyave</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>guava</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kùlàwèíyáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kúlàŋgóó_1771">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kúlàŋgóó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kúlàŋgúá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="kúlàŋgóó_1771_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mygale</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tarantula</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kúlàŋgóó kúlàŋgúá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kulen_1772">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kulen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="kulen_1772_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>igname</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>yam</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.1 Growing crops"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 139: Kulen; Childs 2000, p. 193: kúléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùléŋ_1773">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùléŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kùléŋ_1773_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vol, larcin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>theft</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kùléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùlìó_1774">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùlìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kùlìó_1774_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre, voler (surtout du vin de palme)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take, steal (esp. palm wine)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.4.3 Get"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kùlìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kulle_1775">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kulle</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kullon</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kulun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kulle_1775_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>graine ; graine, semence ; fruit</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>seed, grain ; seed; fruit</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.3 Plant a field"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>seed (generic)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1CO.15.37; Keita 1979, p. 139: Kulle; Childs 2000, p. 193: kúlóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a aussi kulii (1CO.15.38, AMO.9.9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kulon_1776">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kulon</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kulon_1776_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>repas sacrificiels, festins (rituels)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sacrificial meals, (ritual) feasts</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.2 Social event"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>feast, party, sacrifice</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first NUM.25.2; Childs 2000, p. 193: kùlèí kùlɔ̃ŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel. a va kulon dioo nda ndaa « ils mangeaient (les repas sacrificiels) avec eux » (NUM.25.2) ; de kulon o pembon coo « manger sur les montagnes » (EZK.18.11).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kúlú_1777">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kúlú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="kúlú_1777_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en abondance, bien plein</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>abundantly, plump</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>yasala … láà luɛi kúlú taw « des épis gros et beaux » (Gn 41,5) ; la luɛi kúlú « (vos récoltes) abonderont » (Dt 28,4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kúlù-kùlù_1778">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kúlù-kùlù</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kúlù-kùlù_1778_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sursaut (animal effrayé)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>startled jump (of a frightened animal)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 194: kúlù-kùlù</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùlùbèlɔ̀ɔ́_1779">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùlùbèlɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kùlùbèlìá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="kùlùbèlɔ̀ɔ́_1779_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>petit carnivore (genre belette) qui mange les poules</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weasel-like animal that eats chickens at night</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 193: kùlùbèlɔ̀ɔ́ kùlùbèlìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùlúkúlù_1780">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùlúkúlù</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kùlúkúlù_1780_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chaleur brûlante</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scorching heat</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.4 Hot"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>heat</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first REV.7.16; Childs 2000, p. 194: kùlúkùlóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>kùlúkúlù ve lɛnin nda le « aucune chaleur brûlante ne les frappera plus » (REV.7.16). Une seule occurrence.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kumbanndo_1781">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kumbanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kumbannda</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kumbannda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kumbanndan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kumbanndo_1781_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aile</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wing</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>wing of a bird or of an airplane</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first RUT.2.12; Keita 1979, p. 136: Kumbanndo; Childs 2000, p. 194: kùmbǎŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kumbin_1782">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kumbin</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kumbin_1782_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'ouvrir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be opened, open</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.6 Open"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 29 occurrences, first GEN.3.5</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de kumbio « ouvrir ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
