  <entry id="kundaa_1789">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kundaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kundalan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kunda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kundala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kundaa_1789_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>groupe, troupe, camp ; tas, monceau ; (pl.) parts</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>group, company, camp; heap, pile; (pl.) parts, portions</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.1 Come together, form a group"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 86 occurrences, first GEN.17.5; Childs 2000, p. 195: kúndàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>má dii lan kundaa « ils en firent un monceau » (Gn 31,46) ; piɔw … kundalan « diviser en groupes » (Gn 32,8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kùndàá_1790">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kùndàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kùndàá_1790_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>grand, important, honoré</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>great, important, honoured</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.6 Status"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be enough, be plentiful; grow fat</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 86 occurrences, first GEN.17.5; Childs 2000, p. 195: kùndàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Écrit kùndàá dans ce sens : vanaa kùndàá « les notables » (Gn 50,7) ; vana kúndàá bɛndoo « un homme très considéré » (Ex 11,3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kundei_1791">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kundei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="kundei_1791_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>motte de terre ; (parler de Guéckédou) matrice</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>clod of earth; (Guéckédou dialect) womb</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.1 Land"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>cervix</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 8: Kundei; Childs 2000, p. 195: kúndéí kúndóŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita (p. 8) le cite comme exemple de mot dont le sens change selon le parler : « motte de terre » en kisiduei, « matrice » en kpekeduei (Guéckédou), sens proche de celui de Childs.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kunduvaa_1792">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kunduvaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kunduvaa_1792_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>marteau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hammer</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.2 Pounding tool"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>blacksmith's large hammer; also a kind of potion</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JDG.4.21; Keita 1979, p. 159: Kunduvaa; Childs 2000, p. 196: kúndùwáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
