  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛsio_1939">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛsio_1939_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>déposer, poser, placer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>put down, place</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>keep, place, put</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 57 occurrences, first GEN.29.19; Keita 1979, p. 110: Kèsio; Childs 2000, p. 161: kɛ̀sìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛsullo_1940">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsul</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛsullo_1940_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>déposer pour, fixer pour quelqu'un</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>put down for, set for someone</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first MIC.7.2; Keita 1979, p. 110: Kèsullo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de kɛsio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛsɛ-kɛsɛ_1941">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsɛ-kɛsɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛsɛ-kɛsɛi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛsɛ-kɛsɛ_1941_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vraiment, réellement, le vrai ; (parent) proche</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>truly, really, the very one; (relative) close, own</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>actual, real, the very, main</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first GEN.17.12; Childs 2000, p. 161: késé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Nanu ndu kɛsɛ-kɛsɛ Cɛi-Hala-o co nanu « c'est vraiment ici la maison de Dieu » (GEN.28.17) ; vanayɛi ndɔɛi kɛsɛ-kɛsɛi « ses proches parents » (LEV.21.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛvaa_1942">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛvaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɛvaa_1942_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>serpents</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>snakes</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first NUM.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel ; le singulier n'est pas relevé. kɛvaa lólòla nɛyaa « serpents au venin mortel » (Dt 8,15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛw_1943">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛw</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛw_1943_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>refuser, rejeter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>refuse, reject</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(middle adjective) denied, forsaken</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Kèw; Childs 2000, p. 158: kɛ̀ɛ̀nǎŋ-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le radical kɛɛ « refuser » est courant dans la Bible (DEU 27,26), avec kɛɛnin et le moyen kɛɛnun « rejeter ». Mais kɛw y désigne le serpent (GEN 49,17) ; la forme longue du verbe reste à vérifier.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛwvo_1944">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛwvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛwva</text></form></field>
    <sense id="kɛwvo_1944_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>serpent</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>snake</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first GEN.3.1; Keita 1979, p. 136: Kèwvo; Childs 2000, p. 162: kɛ̀ùwɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛ́ŋii_1945">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛ́ŋii</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛ́ŋndon</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛ́ŋun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛ́ŋii_1945_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cymbale</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cymbal</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>bell, iron percussion instrument shaped like a cowrie; hollow log drum</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1CO.13.1; Childs 2000, p. 161: kɛ́ŋndé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>kɛ́ŋun cómulan « cymbales retentissantes » (Ps 150,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛ́ɔ_1946">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛ́ɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɛ́ɔ_1946_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>héritage, part</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>inheritance, portion</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.1 Have wealth"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 186 occurrences, first GEN.15.2</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛ_1947">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="kɛɛ_1947_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>refuser, rejeter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>refuse, reject</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>refuse, disagree with, deny (middle form)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 594 occurrences, first GEN.4.5; Childs 2000, p. 158: kèènɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛlen_1948">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛlen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛyan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="kɛɛlen_1948_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>nervure de raphia, perche (servant de poutre)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>raffia rib, pole (used as a beam)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.3 Building materials"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>raffia, palm fronds (esp. of the piassava palm), swamp bamboo</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 28: Kèèlen : Kèèyan; Childs 2000, p. 158: kèèléŋ kèèyáŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita ne cite le mot que comme exemple de pluriel en -an ; la note manuscrite « Balken » (poutre) et le sens donné par Childs font penser aux nervures de raphia utilisées comme perches. Sens à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛmiaa_1949">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛmiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɛɛmiaa_1949_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>orner, décorer ; plaquer (d'or, d'argent)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>adorn, decorate; overlay (with gold, silver)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.5 Art"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4 Adornment"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 10 occurrences, first LEV.26.1</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen kɛɛmian « se parer » (Jr 4,30). Cf. kɛɛmianɔɔ « décorateur ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛmianɔɔ_1950">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛmianɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="kɛɛmianɔɔ_1950_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>décorateur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>decorator</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.5 Art"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Kèèmianöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. kɛɛmiaa, attesté pour des objets ornés ou sculptés (Lv 26,1 ; Ps 45,9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛsiaa_1951">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛsiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kɛɛsiaa_1951_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>décider, résoudre, projeter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>decide, resolve, plan</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.1 Decide, plan"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first ISA.14.24; Childs 2000, p. 159: kèèsìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mɛlɛka … kɛɛsiaa lende ni « c'est le Seigneur qui l'a décidé » (ISA.14.27). Le nom kɛɛsuula, kɛɛsuulan « projets, desseins » (PSA.33.10-11, JOB.5.12) en est dérivé.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛɛyaa_1952">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛɛyaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="kɛɛyaa_1952_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tailler, couper, diminuer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>trim, cut, reduce</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.3 Cut"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>cut (nails), operate on; clean the tapping hole of a palm-wine tree</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Kèèyaa; Childs 2000, p. 159: kɛ̀ɛ̀yàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme attestée dans la Bible : kɛɛya « arracher (une pièce) » (LEV 13,56), « couper (les ongles) » (DEU 21,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kɛ̀ɲɛ́ɛ́léŋ_1953">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kɛ̀ɲɛ́ɛ́léŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="kɛ̀ɲɛ́ɛ́léŋ_1953_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>anguille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>eel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 161: kɛ̀ɲɛ́ɛ́léŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="la_1954">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>la</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="la_1954_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Pronoun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vous (sujet) ; pronom de la classe lan</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>you (pl., subject); lan-class pronoun</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.3 Pronouns"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11817 occurrences, first GEN.1.11; Childs 2000, p. 220: là</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laalanndo_1955">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laalanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laalan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laalannda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="laalanndo_1955_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>croire, avoir foi, se fier à ; foi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>believe, trust; faith</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2 Think"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>believe, trust; be sure of</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 188 occurrences, first EXO.4.9; Childs 2000, p. 221: làálàŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vanaa laalannda « les croyants, les fidèles ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laalantɛnɔɔ_1956">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laalantɛnɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="laalantɛnɔɔ_1956_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>païen, incroyant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pagan, unbeliever</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Laalantènöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. laalan « croire » dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laalaŋaa_1957">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laalaŋaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="laalaŋaa_1957_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(vanaa laalaŋaa) assemblée des croyants, Église</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(vanaa laalaŋaa) assembly of believers, church</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 42 occurrences, first MAT.16.18</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laandoo_1958">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laandoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>laandaa</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laandu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laandon</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laandun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="laandoo_1958_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>femelle ; de sexe féminin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>female</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.5 Male, female"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.7 Male and female animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 111 occurrences, first GEN.6.19; Childs 2000, p. 221: làándò-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cuaambɔɔ laandu « une jeune fille » ; pɔmbɔ naa laandu « notre petite sœur ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laasi-laasi_1959">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laasi-laasi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laasi-laasio</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laasi-laasian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="laasi-laasi_1959_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dans la confusion, en désordre ; pervers</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>in confusion, in disarray; perverse</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.2 Mental state"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 9 occurrences, first 1SA.7.10; Childs 2000, p. 221: láásì-láásì</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De laasiaa « troubler, corrompre ». yɔŋnun laasi-laasi « être mis en déroute » (1 S 7,10) ; sɔɔn laasi-laasi « paroles perverses » (Jr 15,19).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laasiaa_1960">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laasiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="laasiaa_1960_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>corrompre, perdre ; troubler, confondre (les langues)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>corrupt, ruin; confuse (languages)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.1 Damage"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>mix up, ruin; play tricks, act foolishly; lose, get lost</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 44 occurrences, first GEN.11.9; Childs 2000, p. 221: làásìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de laasian.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="laasianndo_1961">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>laasianndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laasian</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>laasiannda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="laasianndo_1961_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire le mal, se corrompre, pécher ; méchanceté</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>do wrong, be corrupt, sin; wickedness</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 50 occurrences, first GEN.18.20</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vanaa laasiannda « les méchants ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="labɛngunin_1962">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>labɛngunin</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>labɛngu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="labɛngunin_1962_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dessous, en bas ; (o … labɛngunin) sous, aux pieds de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>below; (o … labɛngunin) under, at the feet of</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.2 Top"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>under, between</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 248 occurrences, first GEN.16.9; Childs 2000, p. 14: bèŋù</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="làbɛ́ŋù-níŋndó_1963">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>làbɛ́ŋù-níŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
