      <gloss lang="en"><text>mosquito; gnat</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 136: Muiyo; Childs 2000, p. 254: mùìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le pluriel muiya traduit dans la Bible les moucherons de la troisième plaie d'Égypte (EXO.8.12-14).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mulinndo_2283">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mulinndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mulin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mulinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="mulinndo_2283_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se tourner (vers), retourner ; recommencer, refaire</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>turn (to), go back; do again</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.2 Move in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 15 occurrences, first 1SA.8.8</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mulio_2284">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mulio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>muli</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mulinin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="mulio_2284_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>répondre ; tourner, se tourner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>answer; turn</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>turn over; reply</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 27 occurrences, first 2SA.14.20; Keita 1979, p. 110: Mulio; Childs 2000, p. 254: mùlìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="muloo_2285">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>muloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="muloo_2285_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>impôt, tribut ; rançon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tax, tribute; ransom</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.6 Government"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 49 occurrences, first EXO.30; Keita 1979, p. 148: Muloo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mulullo_2286">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mulullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mulul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mululnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="mulullo_2286_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>répondre à ; se tourner vers</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>answer someone; turn to</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first GEN.45.3; Keita 1979, p. 110: Mulullo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de mulio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="múlúlú_2287">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>múlúlú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="múlúlú_2287_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>réduit en poudre, pulvérisé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ground into powder, pulverized</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.6 Grind"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 254: múlúlú</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mulumulun_2288">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mulumulun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mulumulu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="mulumulun_2288_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se rouler, se retourner (sans cesse), se tordre ; (mulumulu) faire rouler, retourner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roll over, toss and turn, writhe; (mulumulu) roll, turn over</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>roll oneself over; repeat one's words</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first JDG.5.27; Childs 2000, p. 255: mùlùmùlɔ̃ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vana siɛlɛiyo mulumulun o ndu lo kpele « le paresseux se retourne sur son lit » (PRO.26.14) ; O co nɔm mulumulu « il te fera rouler » (ISA.22.18). Cf. mulio « tourner ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mun_2289">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="mun_2289_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Determiner"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ces (pluriel en -on)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>these, those (-on plural)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.3 Pronouns"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.5.1 Here, there"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1752 occurrences, first GEN.1.14; Childs 2000, p. 255: mùŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mundoo_2290">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mundoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>mundu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="mundoo_2290_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>nuque ; dos</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>nape of the neck; back</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.2 Torso"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>nape of the neck</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first EXO.33.23; Keita 1979, p. 132: Munduo; Childs 2000, p. 255: mùndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mungén_2291">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>mungén</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="mungén_2291_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>complètement, entièrement (détruit, consumé)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>completely, utterly (destroyed, burnt up)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.5 All"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 10 occurrences, first 2SA.14.7</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Après cuulu « brûler » ou cuu « périr » : má cuulu mungén « il les a entièrement consumés » (Jb 1,16).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="músúkú_2292">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>músúkú</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="músúkú_2292_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en petits morceaux ; (sable) fin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>in small pieces; (sand) fine</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.1 Small"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 255: músúkú</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="mutarde_2293">
