    <sense id="sii_2967_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>seulement, rien que ; (haliko sii) pourvu que</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>only, just, merely; (haliko sii) provided that</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>only, just</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 18 occurrences, first JOS.22.24; Childs 2000, p. 332: síí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Tueyɔɔ sii ndáà tuei ni « ils entendaient seulement dire » (GAL.1.23) ; Loonun maa hoeiye sii yoomu nuu co ni « souviens-toi que ma vie n'est qu'un souffle » (JOB.7.7) ; haliko sii sɔɛi Krista-e i co diminndo « pourvu que le Christ soit annoncé » (PHP.1.18).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sìì_2968">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sìì</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sìì_2968_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>un peu (temps, distance)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a little (time, distance)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.6 Distance"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 332: sìì</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sììfáá_2969">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sììfáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sììfáá_2969_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rat de Gambie (rongeur qui mange les poulets)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>giant pouched rat (rodent that eats chickens)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 332: sììfáá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cricetomys gambianus.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siilian_2970">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siilian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siilianndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siilian_2970_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'exhorter, s'avertir (mutuellement)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>admonish, exhort (one another)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>advise (plural)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first COL.3.16; Childs 2000, p. 332: sììlìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de silaa « conseiller ». La pɛɛkuan mì la siilian vellaa-velle « instruisez-vous et exhortez-vous les uns les autres » (COL.3.16) ; siilianndo vellaa-velle (ROM.15.14, HEB.10.25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siiluu_2971">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siiluu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siilun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siiluu_2971_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>charger (sur quelqu'un) ; (siilun) porter (sur soi)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>load (onto someone); (siilun) carry, take up</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.1 Carry"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>help with a head load, lift a load onto someone's head</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 18 occurrences, first GEN.22.6; Childs 2000, p. 332: sììlùùwɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siiman_2972">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siiman</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siimanndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siiman_2972_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>égaler, être comparable à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be equal to, be comparable to</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.6 Connected with, related"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first EXO.9.14; Childs 2000, p. 332: sììmăŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vana-vana siiman a Hala le « nul n'est semblable à Dieu » (Dt 33,26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siimian_2973">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siimian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="siimian_2973_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aplanir, rendre droit (un chemin)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>level, make straight (a road)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.4 Infrastructure"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.1 Shape"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plural of 'be equal': be all the same</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first ISA.40.3; Childs 2000, p. 333: sììmìáŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Sans doute causatif de siiman « égaler ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siinguuo_2974">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siinguuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siinguu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siinguunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siinguuo_2974_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire de, rendre, établir (comme) ; consacrer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make (into), appoint, set apart</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.1.2 Do"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5 Authority"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 30 occurrences, first GEN.20.2</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siinian_2975">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siinian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="siinian_2975_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>connaître (des gens) ; (vanaa … siinian) connaissances, relations</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>know (people); (vanaa … siinian) acquaintances</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.3 Know"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1 Relationships"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>know (many things), benefactive plural of 'know'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 2KI.12.6; Childs 2000, p. 333: sììnìáŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de sinaa « savoir, connaître ». vanaa ndáà siinian-nda kpede « tous ceux qui le connaissaient » (JOB.42.11) ; vanaa nda siinian-nda (2KI.12.6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siiyon yiiyo_2976">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siiyon yiiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="siiyon yiiyo_2976_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeu de toupies</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spinning-top game</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.6 Entertainment, recreation"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spinning top; also a gambling game played with tops</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 163: Siiyon yiiyo; Childs 2000, p. 333: sîyé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>siiyon serait le pluriel de siiye « toupie » (Childs sîyé, pl. sîyɔ́ŋ). Dans la Bible, siiyo signifie « scie » (1 R 7,9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sikaa_2977">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sikaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sika</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sikaa_2977_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>douter, hésiter ; doute</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>doubt, hesitate; doubt</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2 Think"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first JOB.15.23</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pɛngi sikaa mà laalan « cesse de douter et crois » (Jn 20,27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="síkítéíyó_2978">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>síkítéíyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="síkítéíyó_2978_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>passoire, tamis</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>strainer</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.1 Household equipment"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 333: síkítéíyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="síkɔ́ɔ́_2979">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>síkɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="síkɔ́ɔ́_2979_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorcellerie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>witchcraft</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.4 Miracle, supernatural power"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 333: síkɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="silaa_2980">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>silaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sila</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>silanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="silaa_2980_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>conseiller, ordonner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>advise, instruct</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>advise or warn</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 105 occurrences, first GEN.26.26; Keita 1979, p. 113: Silaa; Childs 2000, p. 333: sìlàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="silalan_2981">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>silalan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>silala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="silalan_2981_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>préceptes, ordonnances, conseils</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>statutes, precepts, counsel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 79 occurrences, first GEN.49.33</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. silaa « conseiller ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="silanɔɔ_2982">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>silanɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="silanɔɔ_2982_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>éducateur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>educator</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.6 Teach"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Silanöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sílèí_2983">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sílèí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>sílɔ̌ŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="sílèí_2983_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>haricot sauvage (de l'arbre sílɔ̀ɔ́)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wild bean (from the sílɔ̀ɔ́ tree)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 333: sílèí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sílɔ̀ɔ́_2984">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sílɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>sílùéí</text></form></field>
    <sense id="sílɔ̀ɔ́_2984_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arbre à grosses graines oléagineuses ; sa graine</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tree bearing large oil beans; the bean itself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 333: sílɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sim_2985">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sim</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sim_2985_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'arrêter, se poser ; se tenir (debout), rester</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stop, come to rest; stand, stay</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.7 Not moving"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be standing; (causative sìmìó) stand something up</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 461 occurrences, first GEN.8.4; Childs 2000, p. 334: sìmndáŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme longue non attestée dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="símbàá_2986">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>símbàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="símbàá_2986_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tas d'herbes (au défrichage)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>heap of grass (from clearing a field)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.2 Land preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 334: símbàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simbul_2987">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simbul</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simbulaa</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simbulun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="simbul_2987_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enrouler, envelopper ; (sɛbɛ simbulaa) rouleau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>roll up, wrap; (sɛbɛ simbulaa) scroll</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>wrap (up), package; roll up; fold</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 15 occurrences, first NUM.4.10; Childs 2000, p. 334: sìmbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simio_2988">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siminin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="simio_2988_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dresser, faire tenir debout ; planter (tente)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>set up, make stand; pitch (a tent)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first NUM.4.32; Keita 1979, p. 113: Simio</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simisimio_2989">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simisimio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="simisimio_2989_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>superposer, dresser (plusieurs)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>set up, stack (many)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 113: Simisimio</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Redoublement de simio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simlacinɔɔ_2990">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simlacinɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>simlacia</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simlacinɔ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="simlacinɔɔ_2990_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chef, responsable, dirigeant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>chief, leader, ruler</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.1 Person in authority"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 64 occurrences, first GEN.45.8</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simndan_2991">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simndan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="simndan_2991_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hauteur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>height</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.8 Measure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 127 occurrences, first GEN.6.15</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simnun_2992">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simnun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="simnun_2992_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rester (immobile, tranquille), se tenir ; rester en arrière</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stay (still), stand; stay behind</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.7 Not moving"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>stand by itself; change, turn into (middle of 'stand')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first EXO.14.14; Childs 2000, p. 334: sìmnɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de sim « s'arrêter, se tenir ». niaa la simnun yili « vous, restez tranquilles » (EXO.14.14) ; vanaa … kɔɔli-a nda simnun « ceux qui restèrent en arrière » (1SA.30.9) ; mà kɔ simnun o kɔngɔ « ils se tiendront sur le rivage » (EZK.27.29).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="simullo_2993">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>simullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>simulnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="simullo_2993_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se dresser contre, se révolter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rise against, rebel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8 Conflict"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 97 occurrences, first GEN.14.8; Keita 1979, p. 113: Simullo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de simio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sinaa_2994">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sinaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sina</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sinanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sinaa_2994_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>connaître, savoir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>know</text></gloss>
