      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.3 Building materials"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ̀lɔ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔlɔɔ_3156">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔlɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="sɔlɔɔ_3156_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>grenouille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>frog</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 137: Sölöö; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible emploie ŋɔɔŋɔɔnda pour les grenouilles (EXO.8.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔ́mìó_3157">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔ́mìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sɔ́mìó_3157_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>transgresser un interdit coutumier (épier un rite caché)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>violate customs (e.g. spying on a forbidden rite)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ́mìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔmndo_3158">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔmndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔm</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔmndo_3158_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mâcher, manger, dévorer ; (ciŋndon sɔmndo) grincer des dents</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>chew, eat, devour; (ciŋndon sɔmndo) gnash one's teeth</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.2 Eat"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>chew</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 17 occurrences, first EXO.12.4; Childs 2000, p. 338: sɔ̀mndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Childs le cite comme base des formes sòmìó, sòmìlló. nɛɛ caŋndan a ciŋndon sɔmndo vanin « là il y aura des pleurs et des grincements de dents » (MAT.13.42) ; mì la va saa kóndóa téndéa sɔmndo « vous mangez les agneaux » (AMO.6.4) ; le ya sɔmndo « pour me dévorer » (PSA.27.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔmɔɔ_3159">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔmɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="sɔmɔɔ_3159_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>acajou</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>acajou (mahogany or cashew)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 140: Sömöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔndan_3160">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndanndo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndannin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔndan_3160_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'enfuir, se sauver, s'échapper ; (sɔndanndo) aller à l'écart (faire ses besoins)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flee, run away, escape; (sɔndanndo) go aside (to relieve oneself)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.8 Defecate, feces"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>enter the woods (also a euphemism for defecating)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 28 occurrences, first GEN.16.6; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ̀ndǎŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mí Moise sɔndan, mó kɔ viannun o lɛŋnde Madian-nden nin « Moïse s'enfuit et alla se cacher au pays de Madian » (EXO.2.15) ; fondokpaa … le vaa kɔlan sɔndanndo lon « un endroit où aller faire tes besoins » (DEU.23.13) ; Bɔɔle sɔndanndo o co ni « il doit se soulager » (JDG.3.24).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔndɔkɔlɔɔ_3161">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndɔkɔlɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndɔkɔltan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="sɔndɔkɔlɔɔ_3161_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hameau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hamlet</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.6.7 Region"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first RUT.1.2; Keita 1979, p. 142: Söndökölöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔndɔɔ_3162">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔndu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔandu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔndɔɔ_3162_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>coudre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sew</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first EXO.28.3; Keita 1979, p. 115: Söndöö; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ̀ndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif sondul « coudre pour » (GEN 37,3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔngilen_3163">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngilen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngilan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngila</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔngilen_3163_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>coin, angle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>corner</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.3 Side"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.2 Parts of a building"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 13 occurrences, first 2KI.14.13; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ́ŋìléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>sɔngila hiɔɔlulan « les quatre coins » (Ex 25,26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔngɔ_3164">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔlan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="sɔngɔ_3164_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>querelle, dispute</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>quarrel, strife</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8 Conflict"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(verb) fight, argue</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 36 occurrences, first GEN.13.8; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ́ŋgɔ̀ɔ̀</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔngɔ_3165">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔngɔ_3165_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Preposition"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>à la place de, en échange de, pour (compensation)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>in place of, in exchange for, for (compensation)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.4 Financial transaction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(noun) substitute, replacement</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 36 occurrences, first GEN.13.8; Childs 2000, p. 340: sɔ́ŋgɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homographe de sɔngɔ « querelle ». o bɛnda mò ke ndu hɔ́ɔ́yɛi ndɔɛi sɔngɔ hɔlte « il lui rendra la liberté en compensation de l'œil » (EXO.21.26) ; o sala cɔlua nda ŋiɔn sɔngɔ cɔlu pilɛ « il rendra deux bêtes pour une » (EXO.22.3) ; nakɔ … celen sɔngɔ nakɔ nɔmndo ho « une autre vigne à la place de celle-ci » (1KI.21.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔngɔɔ_3166">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔngɔɔ_3166_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>paix</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>peace</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.4 Peace"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first JDG.21.13; Keita 1979, p. 156: Söngöö</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita ne donne pas de glose ; le sens vient de la Bible (Jg 21,13 ; 2 S 10,19).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔngɔɲɔn_3167">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔɲɔn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔngɔɲɔnndan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔngɔɲɔn_3167_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>flamboyer, rougeoyer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blaze, glow</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>dɛngulta sɔngɔɲɔnndan « charbons ardents » (2 S 22,9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔ̀sùàléŋ_3168">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔ̀sùàléŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sɔ̀sùàléŋ_3168_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>canon de cérémonie (pour donner des signaux)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ceremonial signal cannon</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.2 Social event"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 342: sɔ̀sùàléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔ̀sɔ̀ùwó_3169">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔ̀sɔ̀ùwó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sɔ̀sɔ̀ùwó_3169_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>insecte qui creuse des trous dans le sol</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>insect boring holes underground</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 342: sɔ̀sɔ̀ùwó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔ̀sɔ̀ŋàá_3170">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔ̀sɔ̀ŋàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sɔ̀sɔ̀ŋàá_3170_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bourrer, tasser, entasser ; charger (un fusil)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stuff, pack tightly, crowd together; load (a gun)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.8 Full"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 341: sɔ̀sɔ̀ŋàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔva_3171">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔva</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔva_3171_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rouille, scories, écume (du métal)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rust, dross, scum</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9 Break, wear out"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(verb) rust</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first ISA.1.22; Childs 2000, p. 342: sɔ̀wàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Aussi verbe « rouiller » : o nɔla mò sɔva « (où) la rouille ne peut pas (le) ronger » (Mt 6,19).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔvun_3172">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔvun_3172_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fautes, torts ; (cɔm vanndo sɔvun ndɔn) reprendre qqn</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>faults, wrongs; (cɔm vanndo sɔvun ndɔn) rebuke someone</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7.7 Punish"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first PRO.9.8</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel ; litt. « montrer à qqn ses fautes ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔvɛɔ_3173">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvɛɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvɛ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvɛa</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvɛlan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔvɛɔn</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔvɛɔ_3173_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>précieux, de choix, honoré</text></gloss>
