    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vanaa caa sɔɔluuo « les brodeurs habiles » (Ex 26,1) ; doma bɛndu sɔɔlaa « robe brodée » (Ez 16,10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔlɛmaa_3178">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔlɛmaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔɔlɛmaa_3178_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>moquerie, raillerie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mockery, ridicule</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first MAT.27.31</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>sɔɔlɛmaa suiyo « se moquer de » (Mt 27,31).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔmɛɛnɔɔ_3179">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔmɛɛnɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="sɔɔmɛɛnɔɔ_3179_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>brigand</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bandit, robber</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.2 Fight"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 156: Söömèènöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔndian_3180">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔndian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔɔndian_3180_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se disperser, s'enfuir de tous côtés</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be scattered, flee in all directions</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.2 Move in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 25 occurrences, first NUM.10.35</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔnguuo_3181">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔnguuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔnguu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔnguunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔɔnguuo_3181_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'approcher</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>approach, come near</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>approach, draw near; (Liberian Kissi) dress</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 63 occurrences, first EXO.3.4; Childs 2000, p. 341: sɔ̀ɔ̀ŋgùùwɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔsiaa_3182">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔsiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔsiaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔɔsiaa_3182_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sucer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>suck</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.2 Eat"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first JOB.6.4; Childs 2000, p. 341: sɔ̀sàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔsɔɔ_3183">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔsɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="sɔɔsɔɔ_3183_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en secret, en cachette, à part</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>secretly, in private</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.6 Hide"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first PRO.17.23; Childs 2000, p. 341: sɔ́ɔ́sɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>má ɲuna ndu sɔɔsɔɔ « ils lui demandèrent en particulier » (MAT.17.19) ; Ɲɛm kean sɔɔsɔɔ-on « les présents donnés en cachette » (PRO.17.23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sɔɔtɔtɔɔ_3184">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔtɔtɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɔɔtɔtɔlan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="sɔɔtɔtɔɔ_3184_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pourpre (rouge foncé)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>purple, deep red</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 21 occurrences, first EXO.26.1</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Après siaŋa « rouge » : doma siaŋa sɔɔtɔtɔɔ « manteau de pourpre » (Jn 19,2). Dans les listes « pourpre et écarlate », sɔɔtɔtɔɔ rend la pourpre et vólotótoo l'écarlate (Ap 17,4 ; 18,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
