    <sense id="támái_3268_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pièce (d'argent), sicle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>coin, piece of silver, shekel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.6 Money"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 16 occurrences, first 1SA.2.36</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>volii támái « pièce d'argent ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tamalaa_3269">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tamalaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tamala</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tamalanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tamalaa_3269_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tarder, s'attarder ; durer longtemps</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>delay, tarry; last long</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.2 Take time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.8 Speed"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(noun) spending time unproductively, wasting time</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JDG.5.28; Childs 2000, p. 348: támáláá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>la tamalanin le cuvɔɔ « vous ne prolongerez pas vos jours » (Dt 4,26).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="támbàá_3270">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>támbàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>támbàláŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="támbàá_3270_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>petit tambour en sablier (tenu sous le bras)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>small hourglass-shaped drum (held under the arm)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 348: támbàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambálaká_3271">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambálaká</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>tambálakáà</text></form></field>
    <sense id="tambálaká_3271_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dragon, monstre marin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>dragon, sea monster</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.2 Supernatural being"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a supernatural being living under water that possesses people; dragon, jinn</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first REV.12.4; Childs 2000, p. 348: tàmbálàkáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambei_3272">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tambɛi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tambei_3272_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ruine, perdition, désolation ; (kɔl tambɛi) tristesse, regret</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ruin, destruction, desolation; (kɔl tambɛi) sorrow, grudging</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4.2 Trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>poverty</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 29 occurrences, first EXO.10.7; Childs 2000, p. 348: tàmbèí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Nom de tambu « être ruiné ». A sina vɔ maa tambei le Esipte tambu « ne sais-tu pas que l'Égypte est ruinée ? » (EXO.10.7) ; Tambei niaa co kɔlan « vous allez à votre perte » (NUM.14.41) ; o va a kɔl tambɛi le « sans regret » (DEU.15.10) ; dɛnɛ tambɛi « les ravages » (PSA.46.9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambeloo_3273">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambeloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tambeloo_3273_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tambour de guerre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>war drum</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a kind of drum</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 163: Tambeloo; Childs 2000, p. 349: tàmbèlòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambillo_3274">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambillo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>tambilla</text></form></field>
    <sense id="tambillo_3274_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>panthère, léopard</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>leopard</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first ISA.11.6; Keita 1979, p. 137: Tambillo-kuello; Childs 2000, p. 349: tàmbílló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Tambillo-kuello ; la Bible a tambillo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambu_3275">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tambunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tambu_3275_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être ruiné, dévasté ; (tambu kɔl) être dépité, s'irriter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be ruined, laid waste; (tambu kɔl) be downcast, angry</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be ruined, wrecked; rot, spoil; be poor</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 220 occurrences, first GEN.4.5; Childs 2000, p. 348: tàmbéí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Kain tambu kɔl taw-taw « Caïn fut très irrité » (Gn 4,5). Le pluriel est tɛɛmbuuo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tambɛiyo_3276">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tambɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="tambɛiyo_3276_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mardi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>Tuesday</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 152: Tambèiyo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, kɔl tambɛiyo signifie « mécontentement, tristesse » (1KI.20.43) ; le nom du jour est à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tampɔnndo_3277">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tampɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
