  <entry id="tɔ́ɔ́yaa_3527">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɔ́ɔ́yaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɔ́ɔ́yaa_3527_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faute, blâme, responsabilité (bii X tɔ́ɔ́yaa « tenir X pour responsable, blâmer X »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blame, fault, responsibility (bii X tɔ́ɔ́yaa 'hold X responsible, blame X')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first JER.51.25; Childs 2000, p. 370: tɔ́ɔ́yáŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>le yɛɛ Hala kalaa co yɛ naa niko tɔ́ɔ́yaa biyɔɔ? « pourquoi Dieu blâme-t-il encore ? » (ROM.9.19 ; aussi ACT.19.40, JER.51.25).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɔ̀ɔ̀ɲá_3528">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɔ̀ɔ̀ɲá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="tɔ̀ɔ̀ɲá_3528_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire vite, parler très vite, manger ou piler rapidement</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>do quickly, speak very fast, eat or pound rapidly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.8 Speed"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 369: tɔ̀ɔ̀ɲá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɔ̀ɲàá_3529">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɔ̀ɲàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="tɔ̀ɲàá_3529_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>parler vite ; répéter ce qu'un autre a dit</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>speak quickly; repeat what someone said</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 368: tɔ̀ɲàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ̀i_3530">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ̀i</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛ̀i_3530_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>étendre, étaler (au soleil, pour sécher)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spread out (in the sun, to dry)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.5.9 Put"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.6 Process harvest"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spread, esp. in the sun to dry; spread one's hands or legs apart</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 17 occurrences, first GEN.13.10; Childs 2000, p. 356: tèìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mó tɛ̀i malun kullon lecoo « elle étendit du grain dessus » (2SA.17.19) ; ma tɛ̀i nda o dɔ́ɔ́ngɔ́ɔ̀ balɔɔ « ils les étalèrent autour du camp » (NUM.11.32) ; fonda vana tɛ̀i yalalan « lieu où l'on étend les filets » (EZK.26.5). Dans siow X tɛ̀i « tuer X sur le coup » (2SA.1.10, JDG.9.54) le sens est peut-être autre. Cf. tɛilullo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛi_3531">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tɛi_3531_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arachide</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>groundnut, peanut</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.1 Growing crops"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 140: Tèi; Childs 2000, p. 362: tìɔ́ŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, tɛ̀i est un homonyme sans rapport (2SA.1.10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛilullo_3532">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛilullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛilul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛilu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛilullo_3532_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tendre, étendre (les mains) vers ; tendre (la joue) à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stretch out, spread (the hands) to; offer (the cheek) to</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1 Posture"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spread out (e.g. to dry) for someone; open one's hands to someone</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.65.2; Childs 2000, p. 355: tèìlúlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif d'un verbe « étendre » (Childs tèìyó). tɛilul ndu balan « tends les mains vers lui » (JOB.11.13) ; mò tɛilu vana co ndu lɔɔ-o kpannde « qu'il tende la joue à celui qui le frappe » (LAM.3.30).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛiye_3533">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛiye</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛyii</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛyun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛiyun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛiye_3533_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>confluent ; pousse, rejeton ; bras (d'un fleuve), cours d'eau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>confluence; shoot, sprout; branch of a river, stream</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.1 Bodies of water"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.11.1; Keita 1979, p. 155: Tèiye</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, tɛiye désigne un rejeton, une pousse (ISA.11.1) ; le sens « confluent » est à confirmer. Dans la Bible : tɛyii « bras de fleuve » (Gn 2,11), tɛiye « rejeton » (Is 11,1).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ́kpɛ́-tɛ́kpɛ́_3534">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ́kpɛ́-tɛ́kpɛ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛ́kpɛ́-tɛ́kpɛ́_3534_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>un par un, un à un (compter)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>one by one, individually (counting)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.2 Count"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first NUM.1.2</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La cɔm sɛ́lɛ́ Israɛlla tɛ́kpɛ́-tɛ́kpɛ́ « recensez toute l'assemblée d'Israël un par un » (NUM.1.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ̂lɛ́kɛ̀lɛ́_3535">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ̂lɛ́kɛ̀lɛ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="tɛ̂lɛ́kɛ̀lɛ́_3535_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(bien lisse, comme le ciment)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(smooth, like cement)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.2 Texture"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 356: tɛ̂lɛ́kɛ̀lɛ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛlɛlɔɔ_3536">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛlɛlɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tɛlɛlɔɔ_3536_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>surface</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>surface</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.2 Top"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 155: Tèlèlöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛndaa_3537">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛndaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛnda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛndanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛndaa_3537_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fendre, diviser ; (seilen) témoigner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>split, divide; (with seilen) testify</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8 Divide into pieces"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7.5 Trial"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>split, cut open</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 26 occurrences, first LEV.5.1; Keita 1979, p. 113: Tèndaa; Childs 2000, p. 357: tɛ̀ndàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>seilen tɛndaa « porter témoignage » (LEV 5,1) ; bénéfactif tɛndal « témoigner contre ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛndanɔɔ_3538">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛndanɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tɛndanɔɔ_3538_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chirurgien</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>surgeon</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Tèndanöö</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ́ngɛ̀_3539">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ́ngɛ̀</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛngɛla</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛ́ngɛ̀_3539_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>lampe, torche</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lamp, torch</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 32 occurrences, first GEN.1.6</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>tɛngɛla « torches » (Jg 7,16).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛngɛlen_3540">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛngɛlen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛngɛlen_3540_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>roseau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>reed</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JOB.40.26; Keita 1979, p. 140: Tèngèlen</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛu_3541">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="tɛu_3541_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>termitière</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>termite mound</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.5 Animal home"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>chaff, rice straw left after threshing</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 137: Tèu; Childs 2000, p. 358: tèùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le sens « termitière » est douteux : la Bible a tɛwvo « paille, chaume » (1CO.3.12), comme le mot de Childs.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛkpaa_3542">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛkpaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛkpaa_3542_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>février</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>February</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 152: Tèèkpaa</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛlɔnndo_3543">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛlɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛlun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛlɔnndo_3543_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>supplier, implorer, prier ; se plaindre à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>plead, implore, pray; complain to</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 34 occurrences, first EXO.9.29</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛmbua_3544">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbua</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛmbua_3544_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>destructeur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>destroying, destroyer</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 56 occurrences, first EXO.12.13</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De tɛɛmbuuo. mɛlɛkanɔ tɛɛmbua « l'ange destructeur ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛmbuula_3545">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbuula</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbuulan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="tɛɛmbuula_3545_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>transgressions, fautes</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>transgressions, offences</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 70 occurrences, first LEV.16.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De tɛɛmbuuo « détruire ; transgresser ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛmbuuo_3546">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbuuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbuu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛmbuunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛmbuuo_3546_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>détruire, anéantir ; transgresser (une loi)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>destroy; break, transgress (a law)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plural of tàmbéí 'be ruined': spoil, break, misuse</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 176 occurrences, first GEN.19.13; Childs 2000, p. 353: tèèmbùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de tambu « être ruiné ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛn_3547">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛn_3547_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Postposition"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>entre, parmi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>between, among</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.4 Prepositions, postpositions"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.6.5 Middle"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2313 occurrences, first GEN.1.6; Childs 2000, p. 354: tɛ́ɛ̀ŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛndanndo_3548">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛndanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛndan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛndanndo_3548_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mépriser, regarder de haut, se moquer de</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>despise, look down on, scorn</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first GEN.16.4</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛndiaa_3549">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛndiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛndiaanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛndian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛndiaa_3549_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fendre, faire éclater ; se fendre, s'ouvrir (terre)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>split, burst open; split apart (earth)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8 Divide into pieces"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>split; divide, distribute; show one by one</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first GEN.7.11; Childs 2000, p. 353: tɛ̀ɛ̀ndìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de tɛndaa « fendre ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ̀ɛ̀ndo_3550">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ̀ɛ̀ndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛ̀ɛ̀ndo_3550_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>teigne</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scalp ringworm, scall</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>ringworm</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 28 occurrences, first EXO.11.4; Keita 1979, p. 162: Tèèndo; Childs 2000, p. 355: tɛ̀ɛ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible écrit tɛ̀ɛ̀ndo dans ce sens ; tɛɛndo sans ton y signifie « du milieu » (Ex 26,28).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛnduuo_3551">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛnduuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛnduuo_3551_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>couver (des œufs)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hatch (eggs)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.3 Animal life cycle"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>hatch eggs</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.59.5; Childs 2000, p. 354: tèèndùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>A co pelta hɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ́ɔ̀ tɛɛnduuo « ils couvent des œufs de vipère » (ISA.59.5). Une seule attestation.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛngaa_3552">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛngaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛngaa_3552_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire passer, transporter ; transmettre (un message)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>convey, carry across; deliver (a message)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5 Communication"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 619 occurrences, first GEN.20.7</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vana-tɛɛngaa-diom-Hala « prophète » ; vanaa tɛɛngaa « les marins » (Jon 1,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛngei_3553">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛngei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛngon</text></form></field>
    <sense id="tɛɛngei_3553_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>trou, brèche, creux</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hole, breach, hollow</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.5 Make hole, opening"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>hole; burrow (of a rat or squirrel)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 17 occurrences, first JDG.15.19; Childs 2000, p. 354: tèèŋgɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛngullo_3554">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛngullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛngul</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛngullo_3554_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>annoncer, rapporter (à qqn), dire à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tell, report (to someone)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>take (someone) across for someone</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 58 occurrences, first EXO.4.16; Childs 2000, p. 355: tèèŋùlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de tɛɛngaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛnguuo_3555">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛnguuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛnguu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="tɛɛnguuo_3555_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire traverser, faire passer (plusieurs)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take across, make (many) cross</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.3 Take somewhere"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>cross with or carry across (a river); plural of tàŋɔ̀ɔ́ 'cross'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 47 occurrences, first NUM.11.27; Childs 2000, p. 355: tèèŋùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de tɛɛngaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛnuu_3556">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛnuu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛnuu_3556_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dégager, défricher (un chemin)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>clear (a way), clear of vegetation</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.2 Land preparation"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.4 Infrastructure"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>clear an area of large vegetation for cultivation</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.40.3; Childs 2000, p. 354: tèènùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La tɛɛnuu nɛi Mɛlɛka-oo « préparez le chemin du Seigneur » (ISA.40.3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛnɔn_3557">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛnɔn</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛnɔn_3557_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gravier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gravel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 155: Tèènön</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛ́ɛ́nɛí_3558">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛ́ɛ́nɛí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛ́ɛ́nɛí_3558_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>petit caillou, grain (de poussière)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>small stone, grain (of dust)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>small rock or stone; ten large sheaves of rice</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first PRO.8.26; Keita 1979, p. 155: Tèènön; Childs 2000, p. 357: ténéí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>hali tɛ́ɛ́nɛí tasei o cundoo nin lɛŋ « ni le premier grain de la poussière du monde » (PRO.8.26). Pluriel : Keita tɛɛnɔn « gravier » (Childs ténɔ́ŋ).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛsiaa_3559">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛsiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛsiaa_3559_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>interpréter, expliquer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>interpret, explain</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.4 Understand"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 29 occurrences, first GEN.40</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="tɛɛsial_3560">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>tɛɛsial</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="tɛɛsial_3560_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>interpréter, expliquer (à qqn)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>interpret, explain (to someone)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.2.4 Understand"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 30 occurrences, first GEN.41.12</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de tɛɛsiaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="va_3561">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>va</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ve</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="va_3561_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être (passé) ; auxiliaire du progressif passé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be (past); past progressive auxiliary</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.1.1 Be"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.4.1 Tense and aspect"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11781 occurrences, first GEN.1.2</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaa_3562">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vaa_3562_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte, genre (vaa lende « de cette sorte, tel »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind, sort (vaa lende 'of that kind, such')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.5 Type, kind"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 666 occurrences, first GEN.1.16; Childs 2000, p. 377: wàà</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>dɛnɛ kɔlvesɛi bɛndu vaa lende « un si grand mal » (GEN.39.9) ; ɲɛla vaa lende « de telles choses » (1SA.17.39). Homographe de vaa « mille », vaa « cultiver », vaa « être ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaa_3563">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>vàálan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="vaa_3563_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Numeral"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mille</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thousand</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1.1 Number"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 666 occurrences, first GEN.1.16; Childs 2000, p. 377: wàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaa_3564">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vee</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>veenin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="vaa_3564_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cultiver, labourer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>farm, plough</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.2 Land preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 115: Vaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>le vàá « labourer » (DEU 22,10) ; vee, veenin : radical négatif (PRO 20,4 ; GEN 45,6). Homonyme de vaa « être ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaa_3565">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>co</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>va</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="vaa_3565_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.1.1 Be"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 666 occurrences, first GEN.1.16; Keita 1979, p. 115: Vaw</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit vaw (radicaux tyo, vo, va) ; la Bible a le vaa « être » (GEN 3,12) ; vaw y désigne le palmier (JDG 4,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaaliaa_3566">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaaliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vaaliaa_3566_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>devenir aigre ; (dents) être agacées ; (âme) être amère</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>turn sour; (of teeth) be set on edge; be bitter</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first JOB.7.11; Childs 2000, p. 377: wààlàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaalio_3567">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaalio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vaalio_3567_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>maintenant, de nos jours ; actuel (vanndacieea vaalio ho « cette génération »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>now, nowadays; present (vanndacieea vaalio ho 'this generation')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.5 Relative time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first EXO.5.14; Childs 2000, p. 377: wáálíò</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaalɛiyan_3568">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaalɛiyan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vaalɛiyan_3568_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aigre (mɔima vaalɛiyan « vinaigre »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sour (mɔima vaalɛiyan 'vinegar')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first NUM.6.3; Childs 2000, p. 377: wààlɛ́í</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De vaaliaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaan-vaan_3569">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaan-vaan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="vaan-vaan_3569_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fin, léger (tissu) : kola vaan-vaan « voile »</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>fine, thin (cloth): kola vaan-vaan 'veil'</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Toujours dans kola vaan-vaan « voile » (GEN.38.19, SNG.4.1, 2CO.3.14) ; le sens propre de vaan-vaan est à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vaasan_3570">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vaasan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vaasan_3570_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>incisions, entailles (sur le corps, en signe de deuil)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cuts, gashes (on the body, in mourning)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4.6 Ritual scar"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first LEV.19.28</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>keŋnun / kiáŋnun vaasan lekɔɔ « se faire des incisions » (LEV.21.5, LEV.19.28).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vakpa_3571">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vakpa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="vakpa_3571_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>clairement, ouvertement, à découvert</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>clearly, openly, in plain view</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.1 See"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 54 occurrences, first GEN.30.37</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o fula vannda o hɔl vakpa le « il ne monta pas ouvertement » (JHN.7.10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="valaa_3572">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>valaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>valalan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="valaa_3572_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>natte ; grabat, couche</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mat; pallet, bed</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.1.1 Furniture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.7 Sleep"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(sleeping) mat</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 2SA.17.19; Childs 2000, p. 379: wàlàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o ɲɛla hinialan coo a o valalan coo « sur des lits et des grabats » (ACT.5.15) ; cua vala nɔmndo « prends ton grabat » (ACT.9.34) ; maa vala « comme une natte (roulée) » (ISA.34.4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vallo_3573">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vallo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>valtan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vali</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>valta</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vallon</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="vallo_3573_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>travail, ouvrage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>work, labour</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.1 Work"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 137 occurrences, first GEN.2.2; Childs 2000, p. 379: wàlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ɲɛm vallon « ustensiles » (Ex 31,8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="valoo_3574">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>valoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="valoo_3574_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sécheresse, temps sec, absence de pluie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>drought, dry weather, absence of rain</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a short dry spell, a break in the rains</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first DEU.11.17; Childs 2000, p. 379: wàlòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>o tuisi niaa valoo coo « il fera venir la sécheresse sur vous » (DEU.11.17) ; Valoo vanin ni « il fera beau » (MAT.16.2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vana_3575">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vana</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>vanaa</text></form></field>
    <sense id="vana_3575_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Pronoun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>celui qui, quelqu'un (tête de relative) ; personne</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>the one who, someone (head of a relative clause); person</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.3 Pronouns"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2 Person"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 9813 occurrences, first GEN.1.26; Childs 2000, p. 379: wànà-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel vanaa « ceux qui, les gens » : vanaa mandaa n'cɔlua « ceux qui gardent les troupeaux » (Gn 4,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vana lacòòva_3576">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vana lacòòva</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="vana lacòòva_3576_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>menteur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>liar</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>lie, falsehood</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 149: Vana latyoova; Childs 2000, p. 53: cɔ̀ɔ̀láŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mots attestés séparément dans la Bible, mais pas cette expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vana tambɛiyo_3577">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vana tambɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="vana tambɛiyo_3577_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>infirme, estropié</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>disabled person, cripple</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.4 Disabled"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>poverty</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 149: Vana tambèiyo; Childs 2000, p. 348: tàmbɛ̀í</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mots attestés séparément dans la Bible, mais pas cette expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="vana-solia-lasálàá_3578">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>vana-solia-lasálàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>vanaa-solia-lasálàá</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>vana-solia-lasálà</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="vana-solia-lasálàá_3578_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prêtre, sacrificateur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>priest</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.1 Person in authority"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>people involved in initiation ceremonies</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 315 occurrences, first GEN.41.45; Childs 2000, p. 380: wàná-làsálàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Litt. « personne qui offre à l'autel » (lasálàá « autel », cf. fonda-loamaa-lasálàá « autel des holocaustes »).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
