  <entry id="yandɔɔ_3809">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yandɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yandɔɔ_3809_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fleur</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flower</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>(verb) to flower, blossom, bear fruit</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 18 occurrences, first EXO.9.31; Keita 1979, p. 140: Yandöö; Childs 2000, p. 398: yàndɔ̀ɔ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yandɔɔ_3810">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yandɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yandu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yendu</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yandunin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yandɔɔ_3810_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fleurir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>flower, blossom</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.6 Growth of plants"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>flower, produce flowers</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 18 occurrences, first EXO.9.31; Keita 1979, p. 115: Yandöö; Childs 2000, p. 398: yàndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita glose « pleurer » (erreur) ; la Bible (EXO 9,31 ; GEN 40,10) et Childs donnent « fleurir ». yendu : radical négatif (HAB 3,17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yàndɔ̀ɔ́_3811">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yàndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>yàndɔ̀ɔ̀láŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="yàndɔ̀ɔ́_3811_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeune fruit, fruit qui vient de nouer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>young, newly formed fruit</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 398: yàndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Nom dérivé du verbe yandɔɔ « fleurir » (Keita).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yangaa_3812">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yangaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yangaa_3812_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tarder, s'attarder ; passer la matinée (a yangaa kɛndɛ : salutation dite entre 9 h et 11 h)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>delay, linger; spend the morning (a yangaa kɛndɛ: greeting used mid-morning, 9-11 a.m.)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.2 Take time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.1 Period of time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.7 Polite"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spend or pass the morning</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first ECC.5.3; Keita 1979, p. 21: yangaa; Childs 2000, p. 395: yààŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bible : yangaa le, hun cɔ́-cɔ́ « ne tarde pas, viens vite » (ACT.9.38) ; yangaa le len timbio le « ne tarde pas à l'accomplir » (ECC.5.3). Keita : a yangaa kèndè, la yangaa kèndè ; forme abrégée a yangaa, la yangaa. Cf. lɔl kɛndɛ (le matin au réveil), niilu kɛndɛ (11 h-19 h).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yangaa_3813">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yangaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="yangaa_3813_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>crevette, écrevisse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shrimp, crayfish</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 27: Yangaa; Childs 2000, p. 398: yàŋàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita cite Yangaa « crevettes » parmi les noms invariables au pluriel (avec Saa et Nyinaa). Homographe de yangaa « tarder », seul attesté dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yasaa_3814">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yasaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>yasalan</text></form></field>
    <sense id="yasaa_3814_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>épi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ear of grain</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>bunch, ear (of maize), stalk, clump</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first MRK.4.8; Keita 1979, p. 140: Yasaa; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàsàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yàsàá_3815">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yàsàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="yàsàá_3815_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gratter le sol (volaille) ; fouiller, chercher ; taquiner ; danser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scratch the ground (fowl); rummage, search; tease; dance</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.6.1 Search"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.4 Animal actions"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 398: yàsàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yasabaa_3816">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yasabaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yasabaa_3816_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>abri, campement ; atelier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shelter, camp; workshop</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.1 Building"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.3 War"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>temporary cooking site on a farm, before the farm kitchen is built</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first ISA.28.15; Keita 1979, p. 142: Yasabaa; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàsàbáá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita donne « atelier » (p. 142) et « le camp » (p. 156). Bible : refuge, abri (Is 28,15.17), pâturage (Ez 25,5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yàsáŋ-bělló_3817">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yàsáŋ-bělló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="yàsáŋ-bělló_3817_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>régime de noix de palme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bunch of palm nuts</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 399: yàsáŋ-bělló</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yaspe_3818">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yaspe</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yaspe_3818_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jaspe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>jasper</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.2 Substance, matter"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first EXO.28.20</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt au français jaspe ; pow yaspe « pierre de jaspe » (REV.4.3).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yáù_3819">
