  <entry id="yeeliaa_3841">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeeliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yeeliaa_3841_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rendre agréable, rendre savoureux ; faire réussir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make pleasant or tasty; make prosper</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4 Prosperity, trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.24.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de yeela. Mɛlɛka yeeliaa kela ndɔɔ « le Seigneur faisait réussir son voyage » (GEN.24.21).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeelɛiyo_3842">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiyon</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛilen</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛilan</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeelɛiya</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yeelɛiyo_3842_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>savoureux, délicieux, doux ; agréable</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tasty, delicious, sweet; pleasant</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.3 Taste"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.7 Good"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first GEN.27.7</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. yeela « bon, agréable ». ɲɛmahilu yeelɛiyo « un mets savoureux » (GEN.27.7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeemaa_3843">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeema</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yeemaa_3843_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vouloir, désirer, aimer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>want, desire, love</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3 Want"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>also: need</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 22 occurrences, first NUM.16.10; Childs 2000, p. 400: yèèmàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yèèmìá_3844">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yèèmìá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>yèèmìàláŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="yèèmìá_3844_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>interdit alimentaire, tabou</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>taboo, forbidden food</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2 Food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 401: yèèmìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Nom ; le verbe correspondant yeemiaa « avoir en horreur » est attesté dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yeemiaa_3845">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yeemiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yeemiaa_3845_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>avoir en horreur, détester, abhorrer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>loathe, abhor, detest</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>dislike, have as a taboo</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first ISA.1.13; Childs 2000, p. 401: yèèmìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>I yeemiaa bɔɔ lasikɔlɔ niaa « votre encens m'est en horreur » (ISA.1.13) ; dɛnnda vɔɔnnda ya yeemiaa lan « ces abominations que je hais » (JER.44.4).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yéémɔ́ɔ́_3846">
