    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1SA.2.4; Childs 2000, p. 410: yòmìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de yomɔɔ. kpaasiaala ndalan cɔu o yomio « les arcs des puissants sont brisés » (1SA.2.4) ; bala vanaa kɔlvesɛiya la yominin « les bras des méchants seront brisés » (PSA.37.17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yomiyomio_3930">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yomiyomio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomiyomi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomiyominin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomiyomiaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yomiyomio_3930_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>briser en morceaux, fracasser ; (vêtement) s'user, se déchirer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>break to pieces, shatter; (clothes) wear out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.1 Break"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9 Break, wear out"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>break (double plural of yòmɔ̀ɔ́)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JON.1.4; Childs 2000, p. 410: yòmìyòmìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>dɛ̀ndɛ̀la lan la yomiyomi « les navires se brisèrent » (1KI.22.49) ; bala ndɔlan bɛɛ la yomiyomi « ses mains furent brisées » (1SA.5.4) ; o kengelan mó yomiyomi « (le pain) s'est émietté » (JOS.9.12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yomɔɔ_3931">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yomɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yomɔɔ_3931_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>casser en deux, briser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>break in two</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.1 Break"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>break</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first SNG.4.9; Keita 1979, p. 116: Yomöö; Childs 2000, p. 410: yòmɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>yomnin te « ne sera pas brisé » (JHN 19,36).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yomɛiyo_3932">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yomɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomɛilen</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yomɛiye</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yomɛiyo_3932_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cassé, brisé ; estropié (pied, main)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>broken; crippled (foot, hand)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.8.1 Break"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.4 Disabled"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>crippled, lame</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first LEV.21.19; Childs 2000, p. 410: yòméí-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De yomɔɔ « casser ». vana bɛngu yomɛiyo « un homme au pied cassé » (LEV.21.19) ; kpɛ̀ndɛ̀le yomɛilen « un roseau brisé » (2KI.18.21).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondaa_3933">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yonda</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yondanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yondaa_3933_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>proclamer, crier, annoncer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>proclaim, cry out, announce</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>also: call for; complain</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 114 occurrences, first GEN.26.11; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondal_3934">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondal</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yondal_3934_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>crier à, annoncer à</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>call out to, announce to</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 22 occurrences, first JDG.7.3; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndàlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Bénéfactif de yondaa.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondala_3935">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondala</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yondala_3935_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cris, clameurs (de joie, de victoire)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cries, shouts (of joy, victory)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>call, announcement, cry, complaint (yòndàlàŋ pl.)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 2SA.9.10; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Yondala kɔlkɛndɛlan a yondala ɲaalelan « des cris de joie et de victoire » (PSA.118.15). Homographe de yondala « champs » (2SA.9.10), pluriel de yondoo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondanndo_3936">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondanndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yondan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yondanndo_3936_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être proclamé, être annoncé (publiquement)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be proclaimed, be announced</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>shout (middle of yòndàá)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first NEH.8.15; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndǎŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de yondaa « proclamer ». Mí sɔɛi ken i yondan o kobi lebollo Suse nin « le décret fut proclamé dans la citadelle de Suse » (EST.3.15) ; le yondanndo « (devait) être publié » (NEH.8.15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondanɔɔ sɛllo_3937">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondanɔɔ sɛllo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="yondanɔɔ sɛllo_3937_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>muezzin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>muezzin</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Yondanöö Sèllo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. yondan « crier, appeler » dans la Bible.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondo toomaa_3938">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondo toomaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="yondo toomaa_3938_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>forêt sacrée</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sacred forest (initiation)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>men's secret initiation society (Poro), bush school</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 142: Yondo toomaa; Childs 2000, p. 367: tóómáá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Composé non attesté tel quel ; yondo « brousse, forêt », toomaa « circoncision » (dii toomaa, Gn 17,10). Mots attestés séparément dans la Bible, mais pas cette expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yòndònìŋndó_3939">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yòndònìŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="yòndònìŋndó_3939_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(euphémisme) aller à la selle (litt. « dans la brousse »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(euphemism) need to defecate (lit. 'in the bush')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.8 Defecate, feces"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndònìŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yondoo_3940">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yondoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>yondolan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yondo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yondola</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yondoo_3940_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>brousse, campagne, champ</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bush, open country, field</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.1 Land"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.9 Farmland"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>forest, high bush; also the Poro men's society</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 181 occurrences, first GEN.1.11; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>visia yondoa « bêtes sauvages » (Gn 1,24).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yongaa_3941">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yongaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yonga</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yongaa_3941_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>orgueil</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pride, arrogance</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3 Behavior"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.1 Personality"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>pride, boasting</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 104 occurrences, first DEU.8.14; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòŋàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yongban-yongban_3942">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yongban-yongban</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yongban-yongbanndan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yongban-yongban_3942_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(idéophone) violemment, en tumulte (mer qui s'agite, terre qui tremble) ; (yongban-yongbanndan) flots déchaînés</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(ideophone) violently, tumultuously (heaving sea, quaking earth); (yongban-yongbanndan) raging waves</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.3.2 Movement of water"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first EXO.14.21</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoola_3943">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoola</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yoola_3943_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>accorder (une faveur), faire en sorte que</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>grant (favour), cause, bring about</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.4 Do good to"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>help, assist, sanction, bless</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first EXO.11.3; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòòlàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Mí Mɛlɛka yoola mí Esiptea ca Israɛlla ɲia « le Seigneur fit que les Égyptiens regardent Israël avec faveur » (EXO.11.3 ; aussi EXO.12.36).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoolen_3944">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoolen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yoolen_3944_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>liane ; corde, cordon ; vœu ; foulard de tête (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>vine, liana; cord, rope ; cord; vow; head scarf (Keita)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.5 Fastening tool"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>rope, any rope-like material, vine</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 41 occurrences, first EXO.39.15; Keita 1979, p. 140: Yoolen; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòòléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, une corde ou un cordon (EXO.39.15). Dans la Bible, yoolen signifie « corde » (Ex 39,15) et surtout « vœu » (baa yoolen, Lv 22,18). Le sens « foulard de tête » de Keita est à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoomaa_3945">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yoomaa_3945_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vivant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>living, alive</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6 Life"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>live, breathe (verb)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 186 occurrences, first GEN.1.20; Childs 2000, p. 411: yòòmòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ɲaa yoomaa « êtres vivants » ; Le Hala yoomaa « par le Dieu vivant ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoomoo_3946">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yoomoo_3946_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vie, âme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>life, soul</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1 Soul, spirit"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6 Life"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>life, breath</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 129 occurrences, first GEN.3.20; Keita 1979, p. 150: Yoomoo; Childs 2000, p. 412: yòòmòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoomuan_3947">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomuan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="an"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomuma</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yoomuan_3947_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>force, vigueur ; courage</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>strength, vigour; courage</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.1 Strong"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>power, strength</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 352 occurrences, first GEN.18.5; Childs 2000, p. 412: yòòmùléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>luei … yoomuan « fortifier, encourager » (1 Ch 11,10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoomuo_3948">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoomuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yoomuo_3948_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>respirer, vivre ; survivre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>breathe, live; survive</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.1 Breathe, breath"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6 Life"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 2KI.19.30; Keita 1979, p. 114: Yoomuo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>lonin yoomuo « rester en vie, survivre » (2KI 19,30).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yóònà_3949">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yóònà</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="yóònà_3949_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vite, facilement, d'urgence</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>quickly, easily, urgently</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.8 Speed"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 412: yóònà</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yòòndàá_3950">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yòòndàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="yòòndàá_3950_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tendre (bras, jambes) pour atteindre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stretch out (hands, feet) to reach</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1 Posture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 412: yòòndàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoondiaa_3951">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoondiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yoondiaa_3951_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>crier, hurler, rugir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cry out, shout, roar</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plural of 'announce, shout, cry'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first JOB.30.7; Childs 2000, p. 412: yòòndìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de yondaa « proclamer, crier ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoondiaalan_3952">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoondiaalan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yoondiaala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yoondiaalan_3952_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cris, clameurs, acclamations</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shouts, cries, clamour</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first JDG.15.14</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De yoondiaa. yoondiaala kɔlkɛndɛlan « cris de joie » (ISA.44.23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yoongoo_3953">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yoongoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yoongu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yoongoo_3953_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
